# Microsoft Enterprise Features Documentation Policy

## Enterprise Documentation Location for New Features

When implementing new features in this **Microsoft enterprise project**, **DO NOT** create separate documentation files. All feature documentation must be added to [CHANGELOG.md](mdc:CHANGELOG.md) only.

## Enterprise Standards

This is a **multi-million dollar Microsoft enterprise project** requiring:

- **Enterprise-grade documentation standards**
- **Microsoft compliance requirements**
- **Enterprise change management**
- **High-scale production deployment standards**

## What Goes in CHANGELOG.md

When adding a new feature, update the `[Unreleased]` section with:

### Required Sections

1. **Added** - New features and capabilities
2. **Changed** - Changes to existing functionality
3. **Technical Details** - Implementation specifics (timing, dependencies, etc.)

### Example Format

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

### Added

- Feature name and brief description
- New service/component added
- New environment variables or configuration options
- New error types if applicable

### Changed

- How existing components were modified
- Updated behavior or interfaces
- Configuration changes

### Technical Details

- Performance metrics (timing, memory, etc.)
- Processing details
- Cleanup behavior
- Fallback mechanisms
```

## Reference Example

See the image generation feature documentation in [CHANGELOG.md](mdc:CHANGELOG.md) lines 12-30:

```markdown
### Added

- Image generation service using OpenAI DALL-E 3 for talking cat videos
- `ImageGenerationService` for AI-generated character images
- `USE_IMAGE_GENERATION` environment variable to enable/disable AI image generation
- `ImageGenerationError` error type for image generation failures
- Image-based video generation with subtle zoom animation effect
- Male voice support (TTS_VOICE=onyx) for better talking cat experience

### Changed

- Video service now accepts optional `imagePath` parameter for custom video visuals
- Video generation supports both traditional styles (waveform/simple/branded) and image-based
- OpenAI config extended with image generation settings (DALL-E 3, 1024x1024, standard quality)

### Technical Details

- Image generation: ~5-10 seconds per DALL-E API call
- Video with image: ~3-5 seconds FFmpeg processing with zoompan animation
- Images automatically cleaned up after video generation
- Fallback to standard video styles when image generation disabled
```

## What NOT to Do

❌ **Don't** create separate feature documentation files like:

- `docs/features/new-feature.md`
- `docs/guides/new-feature-guide.md`
- `NEW_FEATURE.md` in the root

❌ **Don't** document features in:

- README.md (keep it high-level)
- Separate guide files
- New documentation files

## What to Update Instead

✅ **Do** update these existing files if needed:

- [CHANGELOG.md](mdc:CHANGELOG.md) - Always update for new features
- Existing guide files in `docs/guides/` - Only if the feature extends an existing guide
- [README.md](mdc:README.md) - Only for major architectural changes

## Rationale

- **Single source of truth** - All changes tracked in one place
- **Version control** - CHANGELOG follows semantic versioning
- **Historical record** - Easy to see what was added when
- **Less maintenance** - No separate docs to keep in sync
- **Standard practice** - Follows Keep a Changelog format

## Process

1. Implement the feature
2. Update [CHANGELOG.md](mdc:CHANGELOG.md) `[Unreleased]` section
3. Include technical details, timings, and behavior
4. Commit with feature code

**Remember**: If you're adding a feature, update CHANGELOG.md. Don't create new documentation files.
